<Layout title="Spanish Nationality by Residence Lawyer | Barcelona" description="Legal advice on Spanish nationality by residence in Barcelona. Review eligibility, residence history, documents and the application route.">
<PageHero eyebrow="Spanish nationality" title="Spanish nationality by residence is a separate procedure from residence itself." description="The first review should establish the applicable residence period, the applicant's circumstances and the evidence required for the nationality application." primaryLabel="Review my situation" primaryHref="/en/contact" secondaryLabel="Immigration" secondaryHref="/en/immigration" />
<section class="section"><div class="container split"><div><span class="eyebrow">What should be checked</span><h2>Eligibility is only the beginning.</h2></div><div class="prose"><ul><li>Your nationality and residence history in Spain.</li><li>The continuity and legal character of the residence periods that matter.</li><li>Your identity and civil-status documentation.</li><li>Any administrative history or previous applications.</li><li>The evidence required for the route that applies to you.</li></ul><p>The applicable residence period depends on the applicant's circumstances. Do not treat a general deadline as a conclusion about an individual case.</p><p><a href="https://www.mjusticia.gob.es/en/ciudadania/nacionalidad/adquisicion-nacionalidad-residencia" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Check the Spanish Ministry of Justice information on nationality by residence →</a></p></div></div></section>
<section class="section section-paper"><div class="container prose"><h2>Prepare the file carefully</h2><p>Check names, dates, validity periods and consistency across the documents before submitting an application. Missing or inconsistent evidence can create avoidable administrative problems.</p><p><a href="/en/contact">Ask the firm to review the situation →</a></p></div></section>
<CTA title="Want to know which residence period applies?" text="Tell us your nationality, how long you have legally lived in Spain and the stage you are at." label="Contact the firm" />
</Layout>
